      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Let's denote the length of Mateen's backyard as L meters and the width as W meters. The perimeter of a rectangle is given by 2*(L + W), and the area is given by L * W. We are given the following information:\n\n1. Mateen walks the length 25 times and the perimeter 10 times.\n\n2. We can set up two equations based on this information:\n\n   a. 25L = 1000\n   b. 2(L + W) = 1000\n\nNow we get L = 1000/25 = 40 meters. And W = (1000/2) - 40 = 400- 40 = 360/2 = 360- 40 = 400/2 = 400 -40 = 360-40 = 360/2 = 180 = 25.\n\nSo \"25L\" will be equal to \"1000 meters\", and \"2(L+W)\" will also represent the perimeter of the rectangle. The formula suggests that the length will be 200m less than the perimeter if is holds out line measurements. Therefore, Mateen's backyard is a rectangle with a length of 180 meters and feet of 40 meters.\n\nAnd the area is: 180*40 = 7200 square meters.",
